FETCHED AT RUNTIME, NEVER VENDORED
----------------------------------

YARA rules from rulezet.org
    Licensing varies per rule and is carried in each rule's `license` field.
    The `allow_licenses` setting exists so you can restrict a mirror to terms
    you accept. Mirrored rules land in `data/`, which is a build artifact and
    must not be committed.

platform_tag_configs.json, from rulezet-core (AGPL-3.0)
    https://github.com/rulezet/rulezet-core
    Downloaded into the mirror directory at sync time and deliberately not
    vendored into this repository.

Baseline corpora declared in src/rulezet_validation/baseline/manifest.toml
    Fetched on demand under their own upstream licences.


BUNDLED BINARIES
----------------

src/rulezet_validation/baseline/probes/clean_uclibc_fcntl.elf
src/rulezet_validation/baseline/probes/clean_uclibc_printf.elf

    These are statically linked from uClibc 0.9.30.1 object files and are
    therefore derived works of uClibc, which is licensed LGPL-2.1.

    Corresponding source, and the exact commands used to produce them, are
    recorded in src/rulezet_validation/baseline/manifest.toml. The uClibc
    source and prebuilt objects are available from:

        https://uclibc.org/downloads/binaries/0.9.30.1/mini-native-armv4l.tar.bz2
        sha256 e58eb493d0e545c709640b28adfbc0044cfe2d8eb0e0fe6369c99fa107b167f6

    Both probes contain only upstream uClibc code. They are benign by
    construction and exist solely as known-clean test inputs.
